                    briefing_text_r2:       `The €220M funds roughly <strong>two</strong> bets, not four. Allocate across the omnichannel rebuild (~€120–130M), the data/loyalty + AI engine (~€50M), the hard-discount banner (~€70M) and quick-commerce (€40–90M) — then decide <strong>how</strong> you commit the lead bet. €55M into each builds nothing that wins while rivals spend €200M on one thing. The power of yes is a focused, resourced pair plus an explicit list of what you <em>decline</em>. A tiny pilot in everything is the old maybe wearing a real-options costume.`,
