                    briefing_text_r3:       `Direction is set; now sequence it across 36 months. Lead with the faster, lower-capital <strong>enabler</strong> to bank an early proof point that funds and de-risks the bold build — or go straight for the heavy fulfilment build, or everything at once. Release each tranche on a <strong>pre-committed scale trigger AND explicit kill-criteria</strong>, keep headroom under the 2.5x covenant, and decide when to commit the direction to the market and the 35% family block. The trap: <em>“pilot and reassess”</em> with no gates — staging that has quietly become a maybe.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Defend the yes: the board showdown`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Win a mandate from a split room — two bold directors, two prudent, a Chair who wants a defensible decision, and a 35% family block. The prudent faction asks <em>“why not wait one more year?”</em>; a bold director asks <em>“what if you're wrong about omnichannel?”</em>. Give the prudent enough certainty — gated milestones, kill-criteria, a downside cap — to vote yes <strong>without diluting the bet into mush</strong>. Don't steamroll dissent and don't collapse into a compromise that builds nothing. A direction you can't get a mandate for is a resignation letter.`,

